**Definition (`capMap`).** The map cap map relates basic source and target neighbourhoods by the mathematical operation expressed in its defining relation.

**Definition (`halfIter`).** Repeated halving applies integer division by two the specified number of times.

**Theorem (`halfIter_zero`).** At input zero, half iter has the initial value specified by its definition.

*Proof.* The relevant clause of the recursive definition of half iter zero gives this equation immediately. ∎

**Definition (`bitAt`).** The bit at position k of n is the remainder modulo two after halving n exactly k times.

**Definition (`cupMap`).** The map cup map relates basic source and target neighbourhoods by the mathematical operation expressed in its defining relation.

**Definition (`sumSet`).** The set sum set consists exactly of the elements admitted by its defining membership condition.

**Theorem (`compl_inter_nbhd`).** The construction compl inter nbhd preserves the specified intersection of sets or neighbourhoods.

*Proof.* Use the same witnesses in both directions for compl inter nbhd, combining their inclusion proofs pointwise and using nonemptiness where intersection closure requires it. ∎

