**Definition (`graphMap`).** The map graph map relates basic source and target neighbourhoods by the mathematical operation expressed in its defining relation.

**Definition (`unnumPair`).** Iterating the successor-cell operation reconstructs the pair encoded by the inverse numerical enumeration.

**Definition (`unnum1`).** The first inverse-enumeration coordinate is the first component of the reconstructed pair.

**Definition (`unnum2`).** The second inverse-enumeration coordinate is the second component of the reconstructed pair.

**Definition (`untagRef`).** A tagged natural number is decoded recursively into its finite list of tags and terminal value.

**Definition (`untagStep`).** The state transformer untag step performs one stage of the finite numerical computation encoded in its state.

**Definition (`untagState`).** The bounded tag-decoding state is obtained by iterating the tag-removal transition sufficiently many times.

**Definition (`untagList`).** The untag list is the finite list extracted from, or encoded by, the given numerical data.

**Definition (`untagVal`).** The terminal value of a tagged code is extracted from the completed decoding state.

